      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2012-p10.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By cross multiplying, we can see that \\(MN = 36.\\) Thus, we can make \\(M\\) any factor of \\(36\\) and then determine \\(N\\) from it.\n\nSince \\(36=2^2\\cdot 3^2,\\) we have \\((2+1)(2+1)=9\\) possible choices for \\(M,\\) each of which also determine a unique \\(N.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Cross-multiply the equation",
        "Count the positive divisors of \\(36\\)"
      ],
